    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "## What\nAdd a server-side control over who can use the hosted cloud, and point stable builds at a production control plane instead of staging.\n\n## Why\nThe gate no longer checks an entitled client, so anyone on a release who turns on Developer Mode plus Cloud can spin sandboxes on our bill. Per-org quotas cap the blast radius but there is no allowlist or entitlement. Also, the baked control-plane URL is staging, so a stable release would send all cloud users to staging.\n\n## Current state (pointers)\n- Gate is (env force or toggle) and control-plane URL set: `backend/internal/service/settings/service.go`.\n- Baked URL default is staging: `backend/internal/config/config.go`.\n- Per-org sandbox quota exists but is a single global cap.\n\n## Scope\n- Server-side entitlement or allowlist on the control plane so only approved orgs or users can create sessions.\n- A production control-plane URL for stable builds; staging stays for nightly and dogfood.\n\n## Acceptance\nCloud on a stable build reaches production and is restricted to entitled orgs or users.\n\nPriority: P2. Gate before wide stable distribution.\n",
